  "During evaluation of \
In[269]:=",ExpressionUUID->"431f4d93-ca77-424c-8c65-3941866177dd"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A remark on the zeugon (what it means and why it matters).",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " After the breaking exactly one gauge boson stays massless, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "3"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c10de84-e33e-4d7b-a5f0-24ac7616b4ae"],
 " for the condensate in the channel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K",
     FontFamily->"Helvetica",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "3"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a4bebb3f-d3d9-4b57-83ce-26d0cdcc4f4b"],
 " (in general ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b854e3c7-27ba-4be0-8012-6efedceed4bc"],
 " for a vacuum along ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f6cedfb9-eae9-4e64-b347-744c10dafae4"],
 "), the gauge boson of the unbroken charge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "3"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5293b763-e78d-45a5-a4ac-f41f637aa2dc"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43a2e665-7e74-4016-b240-71cfe0f70b5c"],
 ". It is not the photon: only the DiracLike spinor (charges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c9803349-4314-4f06-b923-a073a069c5d9"],
 "), the bosons ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60b174ce-69f7-4a85-aac4-6bd1eb8273c9"],
 " and the two non-unitary scalars (charges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "106baeb5-e130-4423-8e7d-f708a9e72975"],
 ") carry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a558781-f362-4907-8b5d-c540b7275fc4"],
 ", and nothing in the model carries electric charge. The author, who asked \
for a new massless gauge boson that appears after the breaking and is not the \
photon, offered the solution its naming; the name is the zeugon (from the \
Greek zeugos, a yoked pair), because it is the only gauge boson that attracts \
the two charges of the condensed pair, as the cells above show. Two \
qualifications: its attraction alone would pair the normal vacuum only for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["v",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110f65ec-efad-4bac-980b-e2299acb6d77"],
 " above about 5.3, almost eight times the coupling of the project, so at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0.7"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f8569cbb-6473-4fa7-a69e-021358141403"],
 " it does not by itself hold the condensate, which the pairing term of the \
potential produces; and it is a prediction of the model, not an observation. \
Why it matters: the group that survives the breaking is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a061465a-8c87-4c8d-b6a8-9c372bc9eb02"],
 ", not ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ec6dcc07-c0ff-437e-9569-7f4c137cff16"],
 "; its second component, a rotation by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Pi]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "17401553-ec95-40df-a289-17129ebe033c"],
 " of the isospin combined with the phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c531594-4a50-495e-b623-82901c952f18"],
 " of the fermion number, is a gauge transformation that reverses the zeugon \
and exchanges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "+"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a71ebce-4d11-4751-963e-b84aafa763c5"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "-"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a670d9e-31b2-4255-a365-0e16c336f16a"],
 ", so the charge conjugation of the zeugon is a local symmetry, which it \
never is for the photon. A ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "85cdbdbf-0ff3-421a-9fc4-b4d0056dcc43"],
 " gauge theory with a local charge conjugation is Alice electrodynamics (J. \
Kiskis 1978; A. S. Schwarz 1982; M. Bucher, H.-K. Lo and J. Preskill 1992): \
the vacua ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "0"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[CurlyTheta]"}]], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e546c8e9-7dfe-4ac5-8dba-90098b74ae83"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "0"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"\[CurlyTheta]", "+", "\[Pi]"}], ")"}]}]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fa50332-e2ce-40cc-b795-527b23f87810"],
 " are the same field, so a half-quantum vortex of the superfluid, along \
which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c78beac1-1f2c-4578-9f9e-a7d9faeb1d4a"],
 " turns into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a3e5c77c-8086-44d4-aa81-123ed6ec5cbe"],
 " while the phase advances by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Pi]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29055159-a07d-4a18-9eed-670cc0f18f1e"],
 ", is an Alice string, which reverses the charge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5139ab28-5d28-469f-97c7-fb73cf7fbf2a"],
 " of every particle carried around it (U. Leonhardt and G. E. Volovik \
described its counterpart in a condensate of spin 1 in 2000). These strings, \
and the magnetic monopoles of the zeugon that the sphere of directions ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3479abf9-a676-4cb6-9255-be2c3e9c1ce1"],
 " allows, follow from the topology of the vacuum and are not computed in \
this notebook."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"229baefe-1471-4418-8a97-9762edfbad3a"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Part III, first section. The Landau form of the effective potentials: what it \
is, how accurate it is, and why that matters\
\>", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"95cde7c2-bd64-40f2-907f-0566bc9c5013"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part III of the solution builds the effective Lagrangians ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["CJT",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d203ec2-9a36-4adf-bd73-571685dfe604"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["HS",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10751d21-7728-4faa-a8cd-428a42fe2693"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["KS",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cd59c98-df56-44c6-bb95-e3c0f33a5ed5"],
 " of the field of the superfluid boson singlet state. Their potential parts \
were summarized by a polynomial, the Landau form, with the remark: \"The \
Landau form is a fit; its largest residual is 0.27-0.7 % of the depth\". The \
author asked (21 November 2026) to explain this remark clearly and completely \
and why it is important, to define the Landau form with examples, and to keep \
the answer in the documents and in this notebook. This chapter is that \
answer. It is the first section of Part III in the notebook; the next chapter \
(Section III.T) is the second, and the other sections of Part III follow in \
the next versions. The computed curves are taken from the Rust program ",
 StyleBox["sf_part3",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " (the closed cell of Section III.L.3, with the SHA-256 checksums of its \
data files), and this chapter recomputes from them, by its own least squares, \
every number of the answer; the engine of Part II, which computes such \
states, is used by the next chapter."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15a34be0-1e56-4b60-9a0c-343d65c6e27c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["III.L.1 The objects", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"70eb36e3-d58a-47fc-ad50-cf9158cb21c8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The field and its effective potential.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The field of the superfluid boson singlet state is the complex isospin \
vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "1"}]], ",", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "2"}]], ",", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "3"}]]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c77bb31e-049a-4a2b-8bc5-134eee0e4dcf"],
 " of the amplitudes of the pair self-energy of a uniform state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P",
      FontFamily->"Helvetica",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", "\[Iota]",
     LimitsPositioning->True], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "\[Iota]"}]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["K",
        FontFamily->"Helvetica",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["LL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Iota]"], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a4c0d27d-ff31-4c7f-8c32-4757039f5ab0"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K",
     FontFamily->"Helvetica",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Iota]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bdd3211c-e9ba-4f8c-b00f-04db79df085d"],
 " are the three pair matrices of Part I (",
 StyleBox["kLL[iota]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " in the code) and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "710c3181-6068-4343-a804-327939b74af8"],
 " is one of the five computed methods: HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fe83e6c6-87ef-49e7-8317-f9e44f8a9f1c"],
 ", HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7d7c51-26e2-45b8-bf18-ea9964ec545a"],
 ", HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dd033073-25d6-442a-92d4-a621de763290"],
 " (the method of Hubbard and Stratonovich with the shares ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["HS",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     StyleBox["S",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "45fa29ba-3425-40d3-83ba-06b6e1d3762e"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["HS",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     StyleBox["V",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d5ea1ee-97e4-4c62-b62b-38e8a76b0c98"],
 " of the scalar and the vector term decoupled in the density channels), KS \
(Kohn and Sham) and CJT (Cornwall, Jackiw and Tomboulis). The effective \
potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], ")"}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78a89f6a-4f7c-4e58-ade4-afa63ad76ea5"],
 " is the smallest energy per volume of method ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ee4f3513-3c60-4b83-90e3-51492162b59c"],
 " among the uniform states whose field is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f9da8eac-0491-4329-a24b-33d28d5ebf78"],
 ", measured from the normal vacuum, so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", "0", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bdfc6a73-76bc-4364-86fc-de1365db21aa"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"338c575e-14a1-4d5c-83b4-f87487481eb0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["How it is computed.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A fixed pair self-energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["a",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["K",
        FontFamily->"Helvetica",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["LL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "3"], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3dea6f86-127d-47b5-b904-07f069c73fba"],
 ", the applied field of amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["a",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "92aaa988-b770-4058-8fb2-713ebf9d37fa"],
 ", is put into the matrix of Bogoliubov and de Gennes, the normal \
self-energy is made self-consistent, and the ground state gives one point: \
its own field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    "\[CapitalPhi]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "3"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "61164599-17f3-4915-ba93-f654e0de8ee8"],
 " and its energy per volume. The Rust program computes 61 points per method, \
with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["a",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b915fa03-17dd-46cb-9ccb-37151e57295c"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e540a9f7-3df7-4a85-a0dd-629554fb5967"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d734320c-cdbb-4665-99b9-8a044e0b3f0b"],
 ", each self-consistent to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "13"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "045e2eed-089c-45e0-947e-7bc60be04f6b"],
 ". Along the ",
 StyleBox["polar",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " fields ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[CurlyTheta]"}]], "\[CapitalPhi]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9bbfc309-4074-4aa1-9260-119cdaf4688b"],
 " (real phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[CurlyTheta]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79b8fd67-5416-45c5-9847-04f914bdbe57"],
 ", real unit vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9aac058d-96e8-403f-b18e-9bfcac526e22"],
 ") the potential depends on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalPhi]", "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1296ee93-f98a-46ad-832b-3dc2305c926c"],
 " alone. Its minimum lies at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b2cb9ea-575f-4a35-a35a-ee41c8c68d3a"],
 " (the vacuum), and the ",
 StyleBox["depth",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
       StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ")"}]}], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ab4a1114-d7f2-4f90-a6a6-ea09f7fabb66"],
 " is the energy per volume by which the superfluid lies below the normal \
vacuum. The second derivative ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["amp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "92f17984-c090-4039-81c9-eef09c59f2a9"],
 " of the polar curve at its minimum fixes the mass of the amplitude mode, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["H",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["amp",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]"], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "+", 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3729545f-5ae5-444e-a520-677f4a2d5439"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14f8b428-ed55-445d-ac7e-0c640550fb9a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b6c8586-a5b4-4964-855f-101c3f5cdd55"],
 " are the two coefficients of the kinetic part of the effective Lagrangian."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e5e75eb8-73cf-4832-98aa-4d02dda9896e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["III.L.2 The Landau form: definition and examples", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7d442b2f-3421-4692-9a09-36504a8282c4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A Landau form of a potential is its expansion in powers of the order \
parameter (the field that vanishes in the symmetric state and not in the \
broken one) under two rules: only polynomial invariants of the symmetry group \
occur, and the expansion stops after the lowest orders that bound the \
potential from below and produce its minima. L. D. Landau introduced it for \
phase transitions (1937): near a continuous transition the order parameter is \
small, the free energy is assumed to be analytic in it, and the form is its \
Taylor expansion, whose coefficients (the Landau coefficients) are \
derivatives at the symmetric state. The quadratic coefficient changes its \
sign at the transition; the signs of the higher coefficients decide the order \
of the transition and which broken state is the minimum. Examples:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00ebcbbd-af9b-4328-905b-c5f45088fd32"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A uniaxial ferromagnet: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "90f98c25-79a5-4481-838b-87f4e071d6b3"],
 " for the magnetization ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["mag",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f7b7539-af8b-4422-9c81-f428eb05a62a"],
 " (the symmetry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightArrow]", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["mag",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bb1a7d2f-82ff-4966-a188-abe4d0ed974b"],
 "), with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["mag",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bfa1edb6-2190-40a8-8732-0643dbd569db"],
 " proportional to the temperature minus the Curie temperature and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f8fd34c-12c9-4992-82c7-6c19066a4fb4"],
 "; below the Curie temperature the minima are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["mag",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["mag",
            FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b50ed93-5332-49dd-b752-8efa4a2d1984"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"906c70a8-39ca-4b03-8d55-97275f110632"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The theory of superconductivity of V. L. Ginzburg and L. D. Landau (1950): ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
       StyleBox["GL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
       StyleBox["GL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ddd66de9-3256-4294-9157-15120a0a0552"],
 " for the complex pair wave function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
    StyleBox["GL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "93e464a0-2732-47dd-99fa-e84a682e043b"],
 " (the symmetry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3de2680a-f322-4d41-85bd-b43505d915ad"],
 "), with gradient terms and the magnetic field added. L. P. Gor'kov (1959) \
derived it from the theory of Bardeen, Cooper and Schrieffer near the \
critical temperature, where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "45ae6027-d33c-47f8-8e2c-651e286269a4"],
 " is small; there the coefficients are true Taylor coefficients."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e0f691d2-7dc0-49ab-bc47-a3f2ca02d5d2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Higgs potential of the Standard Model, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Mu]", 
        StyleBox["SM",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "2"]}], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SM",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"(", 
         SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
          StyleBox["SM",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
       SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
        StyleBox["SM",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bbc8cd59-84fd-4880-a471-e90b7253a095"],
 ": the doublet ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["SM",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01652a40-eb9a-4209-83d5-b4156c14b095"],
 " has the single invariant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SM",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "44baf354-f75a-4fb7-a714-a66a4afa8ca6"],
 " of degree 2, and this Landau form is exact at tree level, not a truncation."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"10306a29-acb2-42ca-9aeb-f8c6afb2aa62"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Bose-Einstein condensates of spin 1 (T.-L. Ho, 1998; T. Ohmi and K. \
Machida, 1998), the closest analogue of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "989a0827-d61e-4298-beea-92d5176c32b9"],
 ": their order parameter is a complex vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9423b5fe-4f1b-40d1-b7f7-2cbab98be968"],
 ", and their energy per volume ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["n",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
        OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
        "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
         OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
        "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "81fc8610-7c04-41f8-a2ca-242ee5a51cff"],
 " contains the same two quartic invariants as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "91e6c2c9-bc99-4f04-a8dd-637ce539171d"],
 ", the second term being the square of the spin. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f868881-bbb4-4451-84f5-9947860c11a1"],
 " (sodium-23) favors the polar state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "<", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c742192b-01eb-4701-818c-9039375dd781"],
 " (rubidium-87) the ferromagnetic state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Proportional]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], ",", "0"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4251842e-c059-4878-af33-127fb9f5cf6d"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"07d5f15e-9ec7-484b-bf8c-01437efeca7d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ferroelectric barium titanate (A. F. Devonshire, 1949): ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "6"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d67f2f5-e097-4aeb-9bea-b32f5719e356"],
 " for the polarization ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["D",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aa563a41-dfa7-4ede-ad2b-c38630af331e"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "<", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e6e92712-7d83-47d9-b9fe-1195ea1d413c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "df289674-1446-4523-bcd4-6c8f5401d3b8"],
 ": the sixth power is required, and the transition is of first order."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"16df2a57-a3e0-4ec0-afd2-fca126b126b9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Superfluid helium-3 (A. J. Leggett, 1975): one quadratic and five quartic \
invariants of a complex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", "3"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f407d7d2-a25d-49fc-882e-3348684670bc"],
 " matrix, whose five coefficients decide between the phases A and B. The \
nematic liquid crystals (P. G. de Gennes, 1971): the traceless symmetric \
tensor of the nematic order admits an invariant of the third degree, so the \
transition is of first order."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"65d9f3eb-0828-422a-90ef-187c3a90a618"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The name has nothing to do with the Landau levels of a charge in a magnetic \
field (Section I.6 of this notebook, AS2): the same physicist, another \
subject. ",
 StyleBox["The Landau form of $\\vec\\Phi$.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The symmetry is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[Times]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9cf1d1c2-a88d-41a4-b950-5a668f5647b1"],
 ". The independent invariants up to the fourth degree are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2458aefa-a753-4446-a42b-2a4378232f24"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67277a93-c12c-4b3a-b710-b83d55f2206c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f090db4-9af6-4c1a-b894-51cd37368ad7"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Times]", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "*"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "915b4a11-19af-4585-99a5-a76a55873171"],
 " vanishes exactly on the polar fields. The Landau form used by the solution \
is"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8f9b3fbb-35c5-4259-92c8-b52d5caac70a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[TildeTilde]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "6"], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
       "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
       RowBox[{
        OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
        OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
       "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], ")"}], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"e3611b24-c1da-4f35-8cee-3d5104e11ee6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "the polynomial ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["L",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", "\[CapitalPhi]", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "2"], "+", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "4"], "+", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "6"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e34c5848-27bb-46e2-a1b9-9da949914a65"],
 " along the polar fields. The coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33633e97-9789-4912-976e-b72ca99b6a90"],
 " is not fitted: it comes from the computed second derivative in a \
non-unitary direction at the minimum, and it is positive in every method (the \
sodium case of the condensates of spin 1). The next cell checks, for random \
vectors, that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Times]", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "*"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d51dfc3a-3bcb-4b95-a28e-91465c180468"],
 ", and that it vanishes on polar fields."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7163c090-c210-4e56-a65a-6f3fc9a27991"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"the", " ", "identity"}], " ", "|", "Phi", "|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"^", "4"}], " ", "-"}], " ", "|", 
      RowBox[{"Phi", ".", "Phi"}], "|", 
      RowBox[{"^", "2"}]}], " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"|", 
      RowBox[{"Phi", " ", "x", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Phi", "^"}], "*"}], "|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"^", "2"}], " ", "for", " ", "complex", " ", "3"}], "-", 
       "vectors"}]}]}], ",", " ", "exactly", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"with", " ", "symbolic", " ", "components"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"lfVec", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"lfRe", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"I", " ", 
          RowBox[{"lfIm", "[", "#", "]"}]}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "3"}], 
      "]"}]}], ";"}], "   ", 
   RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Phi", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"lfRe", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{
       "i", " ", "lfIm", " ", "with", " ", "real", " ", "components", " ", 
        RowBox[{"lfRe", "[", "k", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"lfIm", "[", "k", "]"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"lfNorm2", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "lfVec", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "lfVec"}], 
      "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"lfIdentity", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"lfNorm2", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
          RowBox[{"lfVec", " ", ".", " ", "lfVec"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "-",
         " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Cross", "[", 
           RowBox[{"lfVec", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "lfVec", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{"Cross", "[", 
          RowBox[{"lfVec", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "lfVec", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], 
      "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"on", " ", "a", " ", "polar", " ", "field", " ", "Phi"}], " ", "=",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"e", "^", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"i", " ", "theta"}], ")"}]}], " ", "r", " ", "n", " ", "with",
       " ", "a", " ", "real", " ", "unit", " ", "vector", " ", "n", " ", 
      "the", " ", "term", " ", "vanishes"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"lfPolar", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
        RowBox[{"With", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
              RowBox[{"I", " ", "lfTh"}], "]"}], " ", "lfR", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "lfT1", "]"}], " ", 
