Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["How wide is the critical region?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The Ginzburg number is 7.6 to 11.4, far above 1. The condition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["red",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "\[GreaterGreater]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Gi",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a4372e5-aed1-4593-8f4a-d6ea91e65326"],
 " of mean-field theory therefore holds at no temperature where the form of \
Ginzburg and Landau applies: even at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["red",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}],
    TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a6dfcf1f-3f67-45f0-a778-8a6ffd160503"],
 " the Gaussian fluctuations alone give ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["fl",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "/", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["Gi",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], "\[TildeTilde]", "3"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04a25d43-655e-41e2-bb57-1d813fd69e0c"],
 ". The width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Gi",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["c",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ae34ea12-2d7c-4124-90a7-a6304933c33c"],
 " is larger than the critical temperature itself and of the order of the \
cutoff. The reason is in the table: the correlation length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Xi]", 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c71ce5b-ad7e-4459-8406-caa319878125"],
 " is about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e84a8f47-0f2a-45ae-89e1-b89a38e003e5"],
 ", the shortest length of the model, because the pairs are tightly bound \
(there is no Fermi surface, and the pairing needs a coupling above the \
critical one), and the specific-heat jump per correlation volume is about \
0.04, far below 1: a correlation volume holds much less than one degree of \
freedom, while mean-field theory needs many. (In a superconductor of Bardeen, \
Cooper and Schrieffer the correlation length is large against the distance of \
the electrons and the Ginzburg number, of the order of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["c",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], "/", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["F",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}], "4"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7843f8a8-b143-4a31-bc1d-10974c83fe8e"],
 " with the Fermi energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["F",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ee6ba413-db8f-47b0-9a9d-b55fd921aeec"],
 ", is tiny; here the opposite holds.) The error of the regularization does \
not change the conclusion (the last column). ",
 StyleBox["What this means for Section III.T (a remark, and why it matters).",
  
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The statements of Section III.T.6 are statements about the mean-field free \
energy, and as such they are correct and checked. But the temperatures at \
which that free energy shows the behaviour of Landau's theory, from about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0.4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "92e14f2e-dc83-48ed-90c8-ad2e91ad784a"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0.98", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c5dae77d-cb18-4d65-9896-1bed1df94723"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["c",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32aab040-2bf3-4096-816e-5d152f080895"],
 ", lie inside the critical region. The mean-field theory of the five methods \
therefore does not describe the superfluid near its transition: the critical \
temperatures, the exponent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f51384fc-b312-4ccc-bd40-23dfb86b6904"],
 " of the order parameter and the continuity of the transition are not \
reliable. It matters because the five methods agree with each other there, \
and agreement among mean-field methods is no evidence when all of them omit \
the same fluctuations. A reliable description of the transition needs a \
calculation beyond the methods: for example the three-dimensional theory of a \
complex isospin vector with two quartic invariants and with the gauge fields \
on a lattice (the method used for the thermal transition of the electroweak \
theory by K. Kajantie, M. Laine, K. Rummukainen and M. Shaposhnikov, 1996), \
or the Gaussian fluctuations of the auxiliary pair field in HS (the method of \
P. Nozieres and S. Schmitt-Rink, 1985, for pairs bound more tightly than \
their distance)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9936808b-45da-4018-9255-3c8db2e7d844"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
III.G.8 Can the superfluid play the role of the Higgs particle, and is the \
Higgs a composite particle?\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3942c359-adff-4c61-8106-17dbae52f9b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Two questions.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Whether the superfluid can play the role of the Higgs particle has two \
meanings. (b) Can it be the Higgs field of the Standard Model? No, in every \
method, and the answer needs no number: the only matter field of the model is \
the DiracLike spinor, which has electric charge 0 and no quantum numbers of \
the electroweak group ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "\[Times]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8ccb3459-b5f5-4ffb-afd6-d553f10e3efc"],
 ", so every field made of it, the condensate included, is a singlet of the \
electroweak group. Its vacuum value leaves that group unbroken and gives no \
mass to the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3436fbf2-add4-4884-931d-67d68f3d50d7"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ba94c6f-48ca-4495-b825-f2a15d3c2095"],
 " bosons of nature, and its amplitude mode has no coupling at tree level to \
them, to the quarks or to the leptons, the couplings by which the Higgs boson \
of nature is identified. The model contains no coupling between the two \
sectors; a term such as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SM",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Dagger]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "adb1d782-e9c0-4a03-b538-592a3d00dfaa"],
 " would be an addition to the model, would mix the amplitude mode with the \
Higgs boson of nature, and would be limited by the measured couplings of that \
boson. (The first version of this section compared the superfluid with the \
Higgs boson of the Standard Model as if the two gauge groups were one; that \
comparison had no basis and is withdrawn.) (a) Is the superfluid the Higgs \
field of its own gauge group ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[Times]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bf74a814-8844-4093-8d2e-ed49aae4b27c"],
 ", with a Higgs particle? The rest of this section answers (a) with the \
quantities of the new group alone; its scale is not known, and every mass is \
in units of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ad5a576-643e-437c-a864-f7a75af5ec37"],
 ". ",
 StyleBox["The scale of the breaking.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["I",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "413d657f-240b-4c5b-97c4-2db510b48d3c"],
 " with the isospin decay constant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["I",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e481966-f692-4947-a2b2-2ce74ecedf80"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b774bd38-cec9-44d1-a0c4-42c49ec81c80"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "104828f6-b47c-429e-b2ea-71db58f7978f"],
 " are the coefficients of the two invariants of the kinetic part of the \
field, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "+", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Dagger]"], "\[CenterDot]",
        "\[PartialD]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "/", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aa3b6be-2acc-497b-bc11-13c4ece046c0"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b5e5744-5c40-4cd4-bc5f-5977b2c1ad7e"],
 " is the field of the vacuum at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ac7c193f-1c7e-42cf-8269-c0dd71961957"],
 "; the decay constant of the phase is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["SF",
           FontSlant->"Plain"], 
          StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "+", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["SF",
           FontSlant->"Plain"], 
          StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9f7eb1c8-4faa-40ed-8b03-757ec19e44a7"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Z", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a5828628-08db-4aad-a370-e506005ce8b5"],
 ". With the convention ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["gv", "TI"], "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a118bf5a-74ab-4042-8b0f-b19cad1e5251"],
 " by which the Standard Model defines its vacuum value, the scale of the \
breaking and the quartic coupling are"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e3fe264f-8e01-411c-95cc-2ee7676cf220"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "2", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["I",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ",", "      ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["v",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ",", "      ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["H",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ")"}], "2"]}]], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"2ceff785-6656-479e-8a16-273b9e5010d5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with the mass ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f27d8512-860e-4744-acdf-8960f87fc62d"],
 " of the amplitude (Higgs) mode and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["NU",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07946c61-3ad8-4d5e-9aa6-e4d4f9c8fd89"],
 " of the non-unitary doublet from the linear response of Part II (the exact \
small oscillations of each method). ",
 StyleBox["The width of the amplitude mode.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " On the field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
       StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "+", 
      StyleBox["h", "TI"], "/", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           SubsuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["SF",
             FontSlant->"Plain"], 
            StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "+", 
           SubsuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["SF",
             FontSlant->"Plain"], 
            StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]]}], ")"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "0"]}]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "3"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ab8e52ad-df71-4027-8626-9e816980b04d"],
 " (the amplitude field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c4456cf7-e343-4281-a75e-7fc2b07b5f48"],
 " normalized canonically and the phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "0"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39d607e5-4731-4e49-b5dc-1dae79278888"],
 "), and on the same field rotated about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "1"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c1365276-93dc-4e38-9501-b0d9a54eb523"],
 " by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "1"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a295fd7-de88-40ae-bdd5-8956bee652ad"],
 ", the kinetic part contains the couplings ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
       SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "0"]}], ")"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]],
   "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c26f522-9867-454f-9c36-32fb75253021"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
          StyleBox["I",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"], "/", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["F",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], ")"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
       SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "1"]}], ")"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]],
   "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c25c7ca-5d4a-4a7e-b5aa-6c505f9daf52"],
 " (and the same for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0282a1f3-31d3-4825-ace5-312717f543fd"],
 "). With the canonical Goldstone fields ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], 
    SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "0"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "90b1e9b5-3cc1-4ff4-8cc3-fe98fb73ae49"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["I",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], 
    SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b1de8714-c366-4f90-beeb-9e0ae3301904"],
 " all three couplings are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13b5dbc9-d12f-4521-be98-22c2c411ef8e"],
 "; the decay of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f150b8b4-1d0b-45c3-89b7-019b4304108b"],
 " at rest into two massless quanta of one canonical field has the amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["H",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"], "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f4f88b67-dd57-4e7a-a80b-8fbc5f8da74f"],
 " and the width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["H",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "3"], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"32", "\[Pi]", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
          StyleBox["F",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "037404bd-add4-42d5-83ea-6a73d5c5dcd1"],
 " (the phase space of two identical massless particles), and the three \
channels give"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"29a50428-b9d7-4006-a68c-3339e6f7434c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"3", "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
         StyleBox["H",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "3"]}], 
    RowBox[{"32", "\[Pi]", "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
         StyleBox["F",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"]}]], "."}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"23586e45-cfbe-4735-8de1-5e7d7b248354"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With the gauge fields the Goldstone fields are the longitudinal parts of \
the massive gauge bosons (the equivalence theorem of J. M. Cornwall, D. N. \
Levin and G. Tiktopoulos 1974 and of M. S. Chanowitz and M. K. Gaillard \
1985), so that the same formula gives the width into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], "+"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], "-"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "723dc725-2b76-4b6f-b6ea-b1dda7cfd858"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["ZZ", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9cbf04e2-645c-4753-873b-df4107b311b4"],
 " of the new group, up to corrections that the cells after the table of the \
Higgs sector compute. With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f70e9fd-01f2-4549-8e3b-a6a4bcd6c223"],
 " replaced by the vacuum value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["v", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dbcc0564-c8c9-4f25-8487-f19b3dcfba28"],
 " of the Standard Model, the same formula is the known width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"3", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], "3"], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"32", "\[Pi]", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "95f104dd-12c6-40bd-91e9-07fa70a9717e"],
 " of a heavy Higgs boson of mass ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c60df505-2a9b-46d0-a563-ee100beb6921"],
 " into its longitudinal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b5f0e61-427e-4174-b5a5-dfaa670d8b1c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2911edf4-3a74-4886-9bd1-d214ab51018d"],
 " bosons, a check of the normalization. ",
 StyleBox["A remark on the width (what it means and why it matters).",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The formula uses the effective Lagrangian at the energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d3c26b7e-e6ef-4e81-9f58-802a01fb4684"],
 ", where it is not accurate (its mass of the amplitude mode differs from the \
linear response by 7.0 to 17 per cent, as the cell after the table of the \
Higgs sector computes), so it estimates the order of magnitude only. It \
matters because the conclusion drawn from it, that the amplitude mode is a \
broad resonance and not a narrow particle, needs only the order of magnitude: \
the width is 2 to 4 times the mass. The next cell derives the two couplings \
by exact differentiation of the kinetic part (symbolic, with real symbols), \
and compares them with the closed forms and the Rust values."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3d556600-a450-4547-b9ac-e01a64a22677"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
    "the", " ", "couplings", " ", "of", " ", "the", " ", "amplitude", " ", 
     "field", " ", "to", " ", "the", " ", "Goldstone", " ", "fields", " ", 
     "by", " ", "exact", " ", "differentiation", " ", "of", " ", "the", " ", 
     "kinetic", " ", "part", " ", "along", " ", "a", " ", "line", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"gzX", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"the", " ", "field", " ", "at", " ", "gzX", " ", "is", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"gzP0", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gzAmp", "/", "gzNh"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"e", "^", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"i", " ", "gzD0", " ", "gzX"}], ")"}]}], " ", "R_", "1", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"gzD1", " ", "gzX"}], ")"}], " ", "e_", "3", " ", "with", " ",
        "the", " ", "constant", " ", "amplitude", " ", "gzAmp", " ", "and", " ",
        "the", "\n", "   ", "gradients", " ", "gzD0"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gzD1", " ", "of", " ", "the", " ", "two", " ", "angles", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"R_", "1"}], ":", " ", 
        RowBox[{"the", " ", "rotation", " ", "about", " ", "e_", "1"}]}], 
       ")"}]}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gzKin", " ", "is", " ", "Z"}], " ", "|", "dPhi", "|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", "Y"}], " ", "|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Phi", "^", "dag"}], " ", "dPhi"}], "|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"^", "2"}], "/"}], "|", "Phi", "|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"^", "2"}], "\n", "   ", "at", " ", "gzX"}]}], " ", "=", " ", 
      
      RowBox[{
      "0", " ", "with", " ", "the", " ", "coefficients", " ", "gzZz"}]}]}], ",",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"gzYy", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"all", " ", "symbols", " ", "real"}], ")"}]}]}], " ", "*)"}], 
  "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"gzField", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"gzP0", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gzAmp", "/", "gzNh"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", "gzD0", " ", "gzX"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
          RowBox[{"gzD1", " ", "gzX"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gzD1", " ", "gzX"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"gzKin", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ph", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"gzField", " ", "/.", " ", 
           RowBox[{"gzX", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"dph", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"D", "[", 
            RowBox[{"gzField", ",", " ", "gzX"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
           RowBox[{"gzX", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"gzZz", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "dph", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "dph"}]}], 
         " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gzYy", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "ph", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "dph"}], 
             "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "ph", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "ph"}], 
            ")"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"the", " ", "coefficients", " ", "of", " ", "gzAmp", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gzD0", "^", "2"}], " ", "and", " ", "of", " ", "gzAmp", " ", 
        
        RowBox[{"gzD1", "^", "2"}]}], ":", " ", 
       RowBox[{
       "the", " ", "derivative", " ", "in", " ", "gzAmp", " ", "at", " ", 
        "gzAmp"}]}], " ", "=", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
      "with", " ", "the", " ", "canonical", "\n", "   ", "normalization", " ",
        "gzNh"}], " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"Z", " ", "+", " ", "Y"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], "^", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], " ", "of", " ", "the", " ", 
       "amplitude", " ", "field"}]}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"gzCouplings", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Coefficient", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"D", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"gzKin", " ", "/.", " ", 
                RowBox[{"gzD1", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ",", " ", "gzAmp"}], 
              "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
             RowBox[{"gzAmp", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"gzD0", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Coefficient", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"D", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"gzKin", " ", "/.", " ", 
                RowBox[{"gzD0", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ",", " ", "gzAmp"}], 
              "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
             RowBox[{"gzAmp", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"gzD1", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gzNh", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"gzZz", " ", "+", " ", "gzYy"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
       "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gzZz", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"gzZz", " ", "+", " ", "gzYy"}], " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",",
           " ", 
          RowBox[{"gzP0", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<the couplings of h to (d theta_0)^2 and (d theta_1)^2: \>\"",
       ",", " ", "gzCouplings", ",", 
      " ", "\"\< = {f_F, f_I^2/f_F} with f_F = (2 (Z + Y))^(1/2) Phi0, f_I = \
(2 Z)^(1/2) Phi0\>\""}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Do", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"z", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"rustPart3", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<p3_Z_\>\"", " ", "<>", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"y", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"rustPart3", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<p3_Y_\>\"", " ", "<>", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"p0", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"rustPart3", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<p3_Phi0_\>\"", " ", "<>", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
          " ", "g", ",", " ", "fF", ",", " ", "fI"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"gzCouplings", " ", "/.", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"gzZz", " ", "->", " ", "z"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"gzYy", " ", "->", " ", "y"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"gzP0", " ", "->", " ", "p0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";", "\n", 
         "   ", 
         RowBox[{"fF", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"z", " ", "+", " ", "y"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
           "p0"}]}], ";", " ", 
         RowBox[{"fI", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "z"}], "]"}], " ", "p0"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
         RowBox[{"check", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\"\<WP3-H2 \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", "t"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"thName", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "<>", 
            " ", "\"\<: the couplings of h to (d theta_0)^2 and (d theta_1)^2 \
by exact differentiation of the kinetic part, \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", 
            RowBox[{"ToString", "[", 
             RowBox[{"NumberForm", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "8"}], "]"}], "]"}],
             " ", "<>", " ", "\"\< and \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", 
            RowBox[{"ToString", "[", 
             RowBox[{"NumberForm", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "8"}], "]"}], "]"}],
             " ", "<>", 
            " ", "\"\<, = f_F and f_I^2/f_F and = Rust (largest relative \
difference)\>\""}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
           RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "/", "fF"}], " ", "-", " ", 
               "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"fI", "^", "2"}], "/", "fF"}], ")"}]}], " ", "-", 
               " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
                RowBox[{"hgRust", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "\"\<fF\>\""}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", 
               " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"hgRust", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "\"\<fI\>\""}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], 
                  "/", 
                  RowBox[{"hgRust", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "\"\<fF\>\""}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], 
               " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"10", "^", 
            RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<P3-H2 \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", "t"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<YP3-H2 \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", "t"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
       "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "thTags"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ";"}]}]}]], "Input",\

