Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The answer to question (a) for each method",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", judged by the properties that make a field the Higgs field of a gauge \
group and its amplitude mode a Higgs particle."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ba2be281-214d-4cf7-84e0-c1a2316e53fd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The Higgs mechanism.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " In every method the condensate gives the masses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["I",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "babd2b6a-648c-4a8f-b709-cc7a82617c5a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Z", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "98d7d795-ceb4-47d7-abae-55f94c94d3c7"],
 " to the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a493f709-3b9d-4c46-a193-c63e430b2ad7"],
 " and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d9a32145-f1a2-4957-82b3-947088824792"],
 " of the superfluid, leaves exactly one gauge boson, the zeugon ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "3"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e867ab6-afdb-4135-8cae-0fe808d2e35b"],
 " (not the photon), massless, and turns the three Goldstone fields into the \
longitudinal parts of the massive bosons: the superfluid does for the new \
group what a Higgs field does."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"6fbe32f2-a4ef-4fea-887d-36a6330f20e4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A scalar of charge 0 below the threshold.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " In every method the amplitude mode (charge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b063350d-f5cf-4e7c-8061-3f7f6923aa4c"],
 ") lies below the threshold of two quasi-particles, at 0.82 to 0.90 of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["gap",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "372da1ce-2a26-46c8-9572-059ddd7bfbf4"],
 ": a bound state of the mean-field dynamics."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"89d615f8-7dcd-4189-b57f-18be21e52477"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Its mass against the scale of the breaking.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["H",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d396eb0-269a-4cb9-8965-cf4e3c713db4"],
 " is 4.46 to 5.69 and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0dd37031-1add-4e23-be17-160f2d58220f"],
 " is 9.9 to 16.2: the amplitude mode is heavier than the scale of the \
breaking. Whether a quartic coupling of this size is compatible with the \
perturbative unitarity of the scattering of the longitudinal gauge bosons of \
this group is not decided here: the bound depends on the scalar fields and \
the channels of the theory, and it was not computed for this one."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"9bee0ed2-7e6d-413f-ab36-e9ad3d2dba10"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Its width.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["H",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["H",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d2e931a-5464-4cb0-b0e3-4f7c97547b62"],
 " is 2.1 to 3.9: once the decays into Goldstone fields are allowed, the \
width exceeds the mass, and the amplitude mode is a broad resonance, not a \
particle."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"bddb517d-dda0-43d3-abb1-74cf9581ebb4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Further scalars.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Every method has the non-unitary doublet, two scalars of the charges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "1"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b0e1ecd0-7c35-46f5-b58e-3b6d95e0750b"],
 " at 0.99 to 1.09 times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57d5f9c2-833a-454b-ae24-4758e3c41e64"],
 "."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"d6c48e69-8d0a-4d8e-8347-fdc91892f13e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The quantum numbers.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The condensate is an isospin vector of fermion number 2 of the vector-like \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32f9a179-8c68-46e4-a9a1-0f13f5d58bdf"],
 ", a group of the DiracLike spinor that is not part of the electroweak \
theory. The zeugon is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "3"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0efc6703-d7bb-4b09-84c5-d477f3c654e0"],
 " (no mixing angle), the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e7e4881e-d4c3-4508-8605-d9ae19fc6c83"],
 " is the gauge boson of the fermion number, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Z", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6903a5cd-bfa5-4bab-ac42-9d38f5c5110c"],
 " depends on two independent couplings. The mass of the DiracLike spinor \
does not come from the condensate as a Yukawa mass: the condensate adds a \
pairing gap to a Dirac mass that the vector-like theory allows without it."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"7c7e8d6a-f335-480d-a880-5205d357eb97"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The thermal history.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The transition of the superfluid lies deep in its own critical region \
(Section III.G.7); its mean-field temperature, 1.6 to 1.8 times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d69fcf-544e-46c1-8e7a-ebd68a943d1b"],
 ", is not reliable."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"fb62ef29-0906-4113-bdd0-fde84f615c10"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The verdict.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (a) In every method the superfluid is the Higgs field of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[Times]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38cea376-ab50-432a-acf4-4be1e7083b30"],
 ": it breaks the group to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["Q",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70373aec-a0d8-41c0-a8fb-0f00b11a5028"],
 ", gives masses to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c407b75-130b-4d18-ade8-48b57db52708"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d69c940-e5d5-49e4-ab3b-d885fb2834a5"],
 ", leaves the massless zeugon, and has a Higgs-like scalar of charge 0 below \
the threshold of two quasi-particles. That scalar is a Higgs particle only in \
the mean-field dynamics: once it can decay into the longitudinal gauge bosons \
it is a resonance broader than its mass, accompanied by the two non-unitary \
scalars of the charges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b733e0a5-a7b8-4526-80a0-316f308b8013"],
 " of about the same mass. The methods differ in degree, not in kind: CJT and \
KS have the lightest and narrowest amplitude mode, HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74a5c1dc-e71f-4b1e-bafd-a4adda04f6f8"],
 " the heaviest and broadest. (b) In no method is the superfluid the Higgs \
field of the Standard Model, for the reason of structure stated at the \
beginning of this section. ",
 StyleBox["Is the Higgs a composite particle?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " In this model, yes, in every method, for the Higgs particle of the new \
group: the field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bfee52bb-cecf-4067-838c-0c029a86c04d"],
 " is not a field of the Lagrangian, whose only matter field is the DiracLike \
spinor. It is the amplitude of the pair self-energy, a composite of two \
spinor charges; its kinetic part has no term of its own and is generated \
entirely by the spinor field (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3583f92c-9bb4-40e3-978c-e4a38f9572ea"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b4a9b8d3-a106-46fb-a74d-7127e6e5eeb8"],
 " are susceptibilities of the spinor field); and its amplitude mode is a \
bound state of two quasi-particles below their threshold. This is the \
compositeness condition of W. A. Bardeen, C. T. Hill and M. Lindner (1990): \
the normalization of the composite field vanishes at the cutoff, where only \
the spinor field exists. The same structure explains why the composite is \
heavy against the scale of the breaking: in the dynamics of Y. Nambu and G. \
Jona-Lasinio (1961) the mass of the bound state is tied to the gap of the \
spinor charges, while the scale of the breaking comes from a loop of the \
spinor field and is small against the gap. A light composite needs a large \
ratio of the cutoff to the gap, or a different mechanism, for example a \
scalar that is itself a pseudo-Goldstone boson of a larger broken symmetry \
(D. B. Kaplan and H. Georgi 1984). Whether the Higgs boson of nature is \
composite is not decided here, because the Higgs particle of this model is \
not that boson (answer (b)); the measured couplings of the Higgs boson of \
nature agree with those of an elementary Higgs field at the level of several \
per cent, which constrains, but does not exclude, its compositeness at a \
higher scale."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b987372-be89-4d2d-97ae-fccfd9b83cd3"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Part R. The revised hypotheses: the superfluid as the Higgs field of the \
Standard Model\
\>", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"d0c65118-af3d-425e-a55d-b92d36cc030c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On 21 November 2026, at 17:09 PST, the author asked to modify the \
hypotheses so that the superfluid can be the Higgs field of the Standard \
Model, with the same quantum numbers as the Higgs doublet; at 19:38 PST he \
added a second singlet field of hypercharge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox["3", "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06351df5-d4d0-40ab-967c-1f642ee97e59"],
 ". Parts I to III of this notebook state the earlier hypotheses, under which \
the spinor field carries no electroweak quantum numbers. This part states the \
revised hypotheses and repeats, in the Wolfram Language and in exact \
arithmetic wherever that is possible, the checks of the four stages of the \
revision that were computed by Rust programs: the quantum numbers of the \
fields and of their pairs (Section R.1, program ",
 StyleBox["sh_quantum",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "), the ground state of the superfluid (R.2, ",
 StyleBox["sh_superfluid",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "), the masses of the gauge bosons and the modes of the superfluid (R.3, ",
 StyleBox["sh_higgs",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ") and the dynamics in time (R.4, ",
 StyleBox["sh_dynamics",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "). The five remarks made during the revision, R8 to R12, are stated where \
they belong, each with the computation on which it rests, what it means and \
why it matters."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"41ce10ed-302f-4557-badd-a17caff57ac3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
R.0 The fields, the interaction, and how the checks of this part are named\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1d3ace3d-ee85-489c-b274-bee38ceddad0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The fields.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " In the second version of the revised hypotheses, the current one, there \
are three Dirac fields, all singlets of colour and all of the mass ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0.2"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "82187913-b3df-4cde-8bbb-770e4a4dfc9c"],
 " in units of the momentum cutoff ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "98887315-709d-4779-b7a9-3e26ae467e61"],
 ": the isodoublet ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04ea6249-b357-4cf9-b7f6-e99c9f1ca194"],
 ", an up and a down component, each a Dirac spinor of four components, with \
the hypercharge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    FractionBox["1", "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cdb0a80f-6c84-45ae-b9b7-3115395ab49b"],
 "; the singlet ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "feaf1476-885c-49a2-9764-dbf99508d368"],
 ", with the hypercharge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19c9bae7-ddb6-4cc2-b098-7951d3279009"],
 "; and the singlet ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "415ade16-b465-4dff-a995-8a1779cc2fb7"],
 ", with the hypercharge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox["3", "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "93817264-6a4c-4a13-a9c7-971328014160"],
 ". The electric charges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", 
      StyleBox["SM",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68e26bdf-6e47-4147-9c5f-afef43ab934d"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d2901cab-9277-438f-a83b-9b98be359160"],
 " (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "1", ",", "2", ",", "3"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cea2be4e-2359-412f-92e5-1c45b744d158"],
 ") the generators of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d5d026bb-1c5a-4741-b10f-36ad9cfcb52a"],
 ", are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["3", "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "355477be-48ca-476d-af96-8af2c3d126aa"],
 " (up), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox["1", "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "541f8170-7f3b-4b99-b514-78068615c1cc"],
 " (down), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02ea1ed9-e27b-4f30-8b55-35449a80b811"],
 " (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "784b8113-ba6a-4e0f-9ca6-706b649494a9"],
 ") and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox["3", "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2369910c-232d-4579-8b59-0efcc2b2f9a0"],
 " (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57dc414d-6fbf-42b7-baf2-b6de1db569d0"],
 "); antiparticles carry the opposite charges. The first version of the \
revised hypotheses, which this part keeps as the comparison, had no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fecd2a7-5a23-4a8e-a504-9ea5562e7b9e"],
 ". The code numbers the sixteen components of the field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
      StyleBox["LL",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71301464-51b1-44bf-99dd-8c86ff5a9eac"],
 " from 0: the components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "7"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a8a3dfe-d59f-4eff-918e-fd3898f77f23"],
 " belong to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09e6e72e-f6b5-46db-a088-585bab497ed8"],
 " (the component ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50efa36e-7791-4fd5-9892-7c0f094d2c7c"],
 " has the Dirac index ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "0", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "3"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d539b7d6-75e8-4e4c-a40f-867a0366d2c4"],
 " and the isospin index ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a2c01ba-0c84-4967-8287-06947a2a43d0"],
 ", 0 for up and 1 for down), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"8", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "11"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07622175-023d-488c-819e-f42395a12c97"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e40646f-11ce-439b-9410-412ed87c932b"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"12", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "15"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "eb61ce80-ac66-4a8b-a558-c17b09bf38e4"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "db15eaec-63a3-4fca-a195-f2586422bb0f"],
 ". The Dirac matrices are those of the chiral basis, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
       {"0", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["1",
          FontFamily->"Helvetica",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"]},
       {
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["1",
          FontFamily->"Helvetica",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "0"}
      },
      GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
          Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
           Offset[0.7]}, 
          Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
          Offset[0.2], {
           Offset[0.4]}, 
          Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f47f0b43-dabc-4bea-b938-922ffb9afea6"],
 ", with the chirality ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["ch",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "1"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "3"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["diag",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "1", ",", "1"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4144cd91-28f0-450a-8f64-889e28fb7e71"],
 " and the charge-conjugation matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "45c9cd06-b726-40e0-abea-9078c42bfa5e"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d9aeb46d-1636-447f-877a-e58f58c22f0a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The symmetries.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Besides the gauge group ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "\[Times]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b053b8be-0e61-4fa1-835c-7c41b983f1df"],
 ", the free fields have the global groups generated by the particle number \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["tot",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f33f0ef-d1c4-4fe3-90b4-186a9137ac31"],
 " (one for every particle of the three fields), by the relative number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "389feee2-b8c4-4403-9418-e6a9850cd0c3"],
 " (the number of particles of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d751eee8-709e-416a-8a2e-2e724edbd8a2"],
 " minus that of the two singlets) and by the generators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["R",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72f6c125-a573-4b4e-a1e5-501924301b44"],
 " of the custodial group ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["R",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0fd87aaa-32d0-47d2-b725-77213c090f42"],
 ", which rotates the pair ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40d98a6e-f968-420e-80d2-95518c060cd1"],
 " as a doublet. The hypercharge is the combination"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a2fdc126-b782-4853-b1e0-f50109a027d2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SM",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", 
     StyleBox["R",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "+", 
   FractionBox["1", "4"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", "      ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SM",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", 
     StyleBox["R",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "+", 
   FractionBox["1", "4"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "."}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"464587e5-0acb-4261-9be2-bb0963d6eafe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The interaction.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The Hamiltonian density contains the free Dirac terms of the three fields, \
the scalar and the vector contact terms of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d3e9ab3c-b32e-4eb6-8acd-3af238cb01d8"],
 " of Parts II and III, with the couplings ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["S",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"-", "8"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9b96519c-87bf-4ac3-812a-9ee04bb2688e"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["V",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0.8"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c372d1a9-6cf5-4a11-abb6-71eda3eea883"],
 ", and the pairing terms"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"195092c0-f540-4158-b55a-a6eaf3d568bd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["s", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
     StyleBox["u",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     StyleBox["d",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}],
    LimitsPositioning->True], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{":", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
        StyleBox["SH",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        StyleBox["s", "TI"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]], ":", "+", ":", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
        StyleBox["SH",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        RowBox[{"\[Prime]", 
         StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      RowBox[{"\[Prime]", 
       StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], ":"}], "]"}], ",", "      ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["LL",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
      StyleBox["LL",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["ch",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[CircleTimes]", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e",
       FontWeight->"Bold",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]]}], ")"}], 
   SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", "      ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"\[Prime]", 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["LL",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
      StyleBox["LL",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["ch",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[CircleTimes]", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e",
       FontWeight->"Bold",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]]}], ")"}], 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"a8096bf3-288a-460e-b084-95c298c7a748"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "100.8"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c63bd44-0288-43bd-afc8-66767917a386"],
 ", the isospin columns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e",
      FontWeight->"Bold",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["u",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], ")"}], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72313fb6-36ca-4078-8251-8074d3306d7f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e",
      FontWeight->"Bold",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["d",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], ")"}], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c9b974b5-b282-413c-9007-616ddefa91b6"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{":", " ", ":"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4debc183-6dc3-49a8-9603-ac469a1f809b"],
 " the normal ordering with respect to the normal vacuum. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b345ab0d-71c9-4c6e-a04a-4469c1bf9518"],
 " annihilates a particle of the component ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3eb52429-3a8e-48f6-9abe-0bbb140a52a9"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a7b69f37-e918-49bc-b791-aa69df95bce9"],
 " together with a particle of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "065ab7cf-6144-467d-ba86-2732b83e7c03"],
 " in the state of spin zero and positive parity, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"\[Prime]", 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d64d8eb6-7107-4ee8-8c56-42efc4be951f"],
 " does the same with a particle of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08258d4e-27d6-499f-829f-dac9c6a5025b"],
 ". The expectation values ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SH",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["u",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SH",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["d",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d54f52c9-9fe2-4b5c-8c56-2a71d7fb078d"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["u",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], ",", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["d",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "abd1ff72-7b3a-4986-820e-8221c03660d5"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dc82ae2d-6b73-4ff2-95a7-ce58f8ff0776"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      RowBox[{"\[Prime]", 
       StyleBox["u",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ",", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
      StyleBox["SH",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      RowBox[{"\[Prime]", 
       StyleBox["d",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b303b0f5-75ac-4905-9cab-95f67a1ee64e"],
 " are the two pair fields, and the superfluid is their condensate. The \
ground state is computed by the five mean-field methods of Part II: HS (1, \
1), HS (0, 1) and HS (0, 0) (the method of Hubbard and Stratonovich with \
three parameter sets), KS (Kohn and Sham) and CJT (Cornwall, Jackiw and \
Tomboulis)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"96ff1cec-9a04-4352-9e43-2e39dd1b8edd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["How the checks of this part are named.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Each check of this part is one of the checks of the four Wolfram scripts \
of the revision, ",
 StyleBox["wolfram/source/sh_quantum.wls",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["sh_superfluid.wls",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["sh_higgs.wls",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["sh_dynamics.wls",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", under the same identifier: W, the letters of the stage (QN, SF, H, D) and \
a number. The scripts were run on the author's computer, and their reports \
are kept with the data of the Rust programs; this part repeats their code \
with the explanations a reader needs. The checks of the three programs of a \
stage do not correspond one to one: one exact check of the Wolfram Language \
often derives what several Rust checks test in floating point, and a few \
checks have no counterpart. Every check therefore names, after its result, \
the checks of the Rust program and of the Python program that test the same \
statements, or \"none\". In stage 2 the identifiers follow the families of \
the Rust checks (WQN-4 tests statements of QN-4a to QN-4c); in the other \
stages they are numbered in the order of the scripts (decision D34 of the \
task record)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"84575e8d-7ba6-448c-b01c-995991d68575"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A clean slate.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The next cell clears every symbol that Parts I to III left in the global \
context of the kernel, except the functions of the register of the checks \
(Chapter 0) and the tools of this part that it defines. The code below uses \
short names for the objects of the algebra (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8214f4-5e4b-43cf-831a-0c68e4978526"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67415700-6ac3-4513-b28f-c9f549ac4628"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b9e6bf2-1c16-41db-bd30-f002e9670967"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cfa58ff7-a9e4-4ad8-864f-d0268006cc88"],
 ", ...), many of them as symbols without values; the clean slate makes sure \
that none of them carries a value from an earlier part. This part therefore \
needs only the cells of Chapter 0 before it. Each of the Sections R.2 to R.4 \
starts again from a clean slate, as each of the four scripts runs in a kernel \
of its own."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c782cb73-745a-4342-b510-f0e3cf9063ff"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

