Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
R.3.5 Remark R11: in the pairing-only methods the amplitude mode lies exactly \
at the pair self-energy (check WH-5)\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"70c9edf7-455f-4aad-a411-6a533866f05b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The remark.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " In HS (0, 1) and HS (0, 0) the amplitude mode lies exactly at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4760f7ab-661e-4cde-86f2-898571ad06f6"],
 ", below the threshold of two quasi-particles. ",
 StyleBox["Why it holds.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The response of the pair amplitudes along the amplitude and along the \
phase of the vacuum direction has the eigenvalues"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bd301079-487d-4597-9860-a18f39a6fac5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["amp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   RowBox[{"(", "\[Omega]", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"4", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "1"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["LL",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"]}], ")"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["dq", "TI"]}], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]], ",", "      ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["ph",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   RowBox[{"(", "\[Omega]", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"4", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "1"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], 
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["dq", "TI"]}], 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], ",", "      ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "+", 
   FractionBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SH",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], ")"}], "2"], "4"], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"b8b66edc-aacf-44ea-a641-b7eacaf1a8e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "the forms of the theory of Bardeen, Cooper and Schrieffer; a mode lies \
where one of them equals 1. The phase eigenvalue at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "df260eec-f158-41af-9bed-fbe9381d4b44"],
 " is the gap equation, so it equals 1 there: the Goldstone mode. The \
identity of the integrands, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"]}], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
        SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]], "-", 
    FractionBox["1", 
     StyleBox["E", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"]}], 
     RowBox[{"4", 
      StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
        SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5a7c272b-ceab-45e8-94fb-2d2181c09cc5"],
 ", gives"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d956b8e0-0f17-4f11-85a1-02b93158e1cd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["amp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   RowBox[{"(", "\[Omega]", ")"}], "-", "1", "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SH",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], ")"}], "2"]}], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"4", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "1"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["q", "TI"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["dq", "TI"]}], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"b0d6ac21-fbe9-4c03-8d67-edfb40c71e83"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "and the integral is positive below the threshold ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["eff",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"4", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["LL",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "+", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"(", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["SH",
           FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], ")"}], "2"]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8243c4ff-aac2-406d-b633-7a1c230a6c6a"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "/", "4", ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5220ab1a-83f7-4e1f-9f12-51748bf765c9"],
 " for every momentum. So ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["amp",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f9350ad-4138-4666-b40b-0fff89ece1f7"],
 " only at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4884a079-c06f-40c7-a8f6-3269e484c943"],
 ", for every coupling, mass and cutoff. The cell proves the identity and the \
positivity symbolically (the latter by deciding a statement about all real \
numbers), evaluates the integrals with 30 digits, finds the root of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["amp",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "974cade1-6da0-486c-ab0e-188eb4702199"],
 " and compares the frequencies that the Rust program found from the linear \
response of the whole sector, without the closed forms. The two closed forms \
themselves were found by comparison with the response of the Python program, \
not derived by hand. ",
 StyleBox["Why it matters.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (1) It is the result of the theory of Bardeen, Cooper and Schrieffer, in \
which the amplitude mode lies at twice the gap parameter; here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f12c59e7-bf7f-4604-a4a7-56e7b4674803"],
 " plays that role, and the mass ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16c374b3-7ff2-4543-945a-655724ccef0a"],
 " raises the lowest quasi-particle energy to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["eff",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "61da72fd-bf52-4317-9618-3f30f477d200"],
 ", so that the mode is bound below the threshold, a sharp particle of the \
mean field. (2) It fixes the mass of the candidate for the Higgs boson: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "/", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], "/", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SH",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f3bc6054-6be1-48f9-981e-50b1931249d1"],
 ", about 8 in the second version against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["H", "TI"]], "/", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "\[TildeTilde]", "0.51"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "074d04e9-7956-4e4b-809f-442065e6e0ca"],
 " in the Standard Model (check WH-4). (3) The effective Lagrangian fails \
here: it gives a frequency above the threshold, because an expansion in the \
frequency cannot hold for a mode so close to it. (4) The mode at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SH",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "28b37303-51e8-4179-807b-3fd122e90219"],
 " holds in the time domain too (Section R.4), and only in the pairing-only \
methods: with the scalar and the vector terms, HS (1, 1) puts it somewhat \
lower, still bound, and KS and CJT put it above the energy that breaks a \
pair, where it decays. (5) It is a mean-field result; the fluctuations beyond \
the mean field are not computed."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c04cb290-d328-4320-8a96-532d8db4a1c8"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"--", 
       RowBox[{"--", 
        RowBox[{"--", 
         RowBox[{"--", 
          RowBox[{"--", 
           RowBox[{"--", 
            RowBox[{"--", 
             RowBox[{"--", 
              RowBox[{"--", 
               RowBox[{"--", 
                RowBox[{"--", 
                 RowBox[{"--", 
                  RowBox[{"--", 
                   RowBox[{"--", 
                    RowBox[{"--", 
                    RowBox[{"--", 
                    RowBox[{"--", 
                    RowBox[{"--", 
                    RowBox[{"--", 
                    RowBox[{"--", 
